Z||000007||Black88GT||08-02-2001||01:41 AM||||What the hell is so important about a horn anyway???? Never understood this one.  Not too many people I know would say "Dude, have you seen that new C6 Concept? I wonder what the horn sounds like?"  or "Man, your car might be faster, handle better, and look better, but my horn sounds soooo much better then yours"  ||||reg||1
Z||000008||Coop88||08-02-2001||06:05 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Black88GT:<BR><B>What the hell is so important about a horn anyway???? Never understood this one.  Not too many people I know would say "Dude, have you seen that new C6 Concept? I wonder what the horn sounds like?"  or "Man, your car might be faster, handle better, and look better, but my horn sounds soooo much better then yours"  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I would feel more satisfied having a louder, deeper sounding horn. The Fiero's horn is so high pitched and quiet it sounds friendly. Good to use when I see another Fiero driving around, not so good when some moron pulls right out in front of me or nearly runs me off the road(I wonder how some people passed their driving test). In one of Four-Banger's threads it is mentioned that the family dog thinks the Fiero is a squeak toy because of the horn. I guess what I'm saying is if you took two identical Fiero's(except for the horn) and Fiero #1 sounded stock, and Fiero #2 sounded like a semi, the second fiero would motivate more people to get out of the way. Also, I would relieve more anger/aggression in Fiero #2. That's just my $.02. <P>Edit: I would not buy a car based on the sound of the horn. A louder horn would be a bonus. Lisa, I have no idea what the decible level of the stock horn is. You can get a 130db horn at harborfrieght.com. <p>[This message has been edited by Coop88 (edited 08-02-2001).]||||reg||12
Z||000009||Lisa 86 2m4||08-02-2001||07:52 PM||||Ditto that. I had a very close call on the highway the the other day, prompting this new search on horns, where a truck decided it wanted to be in my lane, while I was still in it. Needless to say the horn did very little to alert the driver requiring me to bite the shoulder and slam on the brakes. I think if the horn was a little louder than a squeak toy it might not have been such a close call.  Thanks for the idea of pulling one out of the junk yard.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000010||theogre||08-02-2001||08:09 PM||||Knowing GM, they are no louder than the FMVSS rules require.<P>you can get the link to the FMVSS standards from my brake fluid article. I don't know if horns are listed in their own section or not. I haven't read the whole mess.||||reg||1
